beretta tunberg is a hero to this  generation of climate change activists  for weeks he's been Criss crossing  America adding star power to the youth  climate strikes here in Los Angeles she  marched with students to protest the  city's continued drilling for oil and  the polluting effects on young people's  lives and the bigger message on the need  to tackle climate change they're taking  this message directly to the politicians  here in California because they know  that here they're preaching to the  converted they need to get this message  out to a more skeptical public she has  mobilized a movement here I think it's  very important because she shows that  kids can stand up for these things as  well and that our generation is the ones  that this is going to affect the most  and having her as the voice for young  kids is really good Greta started  speaking about like we need to focus on  this now and we only have like a few  years left to make a change so I  actually started to like we started  going to events like these and started  taking action now a lot of young people  feel like we don't have a voice so it's  definitely very important to have  someone like her to show us that we do  matter because this is our future the  protest came as Californians faced what  many see is a byproduct of the changing  climate the terrifying wind driven  wildfires burning across the state and  turning lives upside-down a new fire 75  miles north of Los Angeles has prompted  more evacuations more homes have burned  in what's been four firefighters a  relentless slog in recent weeks the  protesters want California's governor to  do more on climate change earlier this  week he told Sky News the fires were a  direct result if you don't believe in  science they don't believe in climate  change  but you have to believe in your own eyes  observed reality and you come to  California and you go through that five  year drought and then you have this  these atmospheric rivers and rain falls  likes of which you've never seen in  floods and forgive the vernacular but  something ain't right today in  California we can see the wildfires  happening just around the corner  wildfires that are being intensified by  the climate crisis young protesters say  they won't stop until the world takes  notice and takes action on what they say  is a global crisis which should concern  us all Greg Milan Sky News Los Angeles  [Music]
 

